<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>

<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "dwtldr">
<!ENTITY author    "desertwitch">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.10.16">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&author;/tldr-unRAID/main">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/plugin/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY pkgURL    "&gitURL;/packages">
<!ENTITY plgPATH   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/171110-plugin-tldr-command-line-cheatsheets-for-unraid/" min="6.10.0" icon="quote-left">

<CHANGES>
## TLDR (Command-Line Cheatsheets) for UNRAID
###2026.10.16
#### Plugin Advisory: End of Support on 30.11.2026
With new details on Unraid 8 now available, it felt like the right time to make a final decision about this plugin and set clear expectations. I've been focused on new things for a while and am preparing the transition of my own infrastructure, so I can no longer give the plugin the attention and love it deserves. It wasn't an easy choice, but support will end on 30.11.2026. From that date, the plugin stays installable as-is, but without any guarantee of stability or usability, so use is entirely at your own risk. The repository will be archived, but if a future Unraid release is reported to break the plugin in the support thread, I'll have to cap the maximum supported version and prevent further installs from that version onwards. Forks are very welcome; just coordinate with the Community Applications maintainers. Thank you all for the support over the years - Unraid has been an amazing community to serve, and I hope to stay in touch with many of you on the forums or Discord.
###2026.10.06
- announce maintenance mode (no functional changes)
###2026.05.01b
- new: updated tlrc package to latest release version (v1.13.0)
###2024.09.14
- new: updated tlrc package to latest release version (v1.9.3)
###2024.07.26
- release note: welcome to the first version of the package
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
killall tldr >/dev/null 2>&amp;1
exit 0
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&plgPATH;/tlrc-1.13.0-x86_64-1dw.txz" Min="6.10.0" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&pkgURL;/tlrc-1.13.0-x86_64-1dw.txz</URL>
<MD5>12df236f947842f7a45675bb2b058675</MD5>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/README.md" Mode="0644">
<INLINE>
**TLDR (Command-Line Cheatsheets) for UNRAID**

Simplified and community-driven manpages / Terminal Command: **tldr** / User Manual: **tldr --help**
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
echo ""
echo "-------------------------------------------------------------"
echo " TLDR (Command-Line Cheatsheets) for UNRAID has been installed."
echo " Version: &version; / Plugin Maintainer: &author;"
echo "-------------------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
killall tldr >/dev/null 2>&amp;1
removepkg &plgPATH;/*.txz
rm -rf /root/.cache/tlrc
rm -rf /root/.config/tlrc
rm -rf &plgPATH;
rm -rf &emhttp;
echo ""
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo " TLDR (Command-Line Cheatsheets) for UNRAID has been removed."
echo " Version: &version; / Plugin Maintainer: &author;"
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
